The Standard Model of particle physics has 26 free parameters. It cannot derive the particle spectrum — the masses of the quarks and leptons are inputs.

The WIN Paradigm (Preschutti 2026) derives the Standard Model's gauge structure and matter content from a single input: `d = 4`. The framework identifies the substrate as an 8×8 torus with a 14-fold degeneracy at λ = 4, matching the Standard Model's 14 particles.

Each mode has an associated quantity N/4 that orders the particles by mass. The N/4 values are:

```
60, 24, 21, 20, 14, 14, 12, 9.5, 9, 7.5, 2, 2, 1, 0.5
```

The ordering correlates with entropy at Spearman 0.998, but the magnitudes are not derived.

This paper presents a derivation of the N/4 values from the mode structure.

